<section id="" data-section-id="rzOTmkaByX" data-section="story-9" data-dev="hongyen" data-lh-page-id="1469" data-lh-page-name="Happier Every Chapter - About Us" data-layouthub="section">  
 <section id='lh-about-intro' class='lh-section lh-about-intro'>
  <div class='lh-container'><div class='lh-row'><div class='lh-col-md-12'>
    <div class='lh-about-intro__content'>
      <h2  data-lhi="txt_title" data-lh-lang>{{ 'rzOTmkaByX.lh_a168_title' | t }}</h2>
      <div class='lh-richtext'  data-lhi="txt_body" data-lh-lang data-lh-live-editor><p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Many children lack access to diverse and inclusive books that reflect the world around them. This can make reading less engaging for some children and leave families, schools and libraries with limited access to stories that celebrate different cultures, identities and experiences. Happier Every Chapter was created to help solve this problem through carefully curated children's book subscriptions for ages 0–14, promoting reading for pleasure while helping every child feel seen, valued and represented.<br><br>Welcome to Happier Every Chapter!</span> Pictured above are <span style="font-weight: bold;">Kirsten </span> and <span style="font-weight: bold;">Aiyven</span><span style="font-weight: bold;">, <a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-northamptonshire-62742503">the First Ever Young Female Leads</a></span>. They are how our story started. Voracious readers &amp; talented writers, with a bit of a thing for getting others to catch the bug too☺. <span style="font-weight: bold;">Sagas of Anya</span> by Kirsten &amp; Land Of The Nurogons by Aiyven are their debut novels which came to be as entries to the 2019 BBC 500 Words writing competition. Not to be deterred because they didn't win, they turned our entries into middle-grade novels, published in April 2020 with the help of a <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/mbawabooks/land-of-the-nurogons-and-sagas-of-anya?ref=discovery_staff_picks_location">Kickstarter campaign</a>.<br>&nbsp;<br>You may have watched their YouTube book reviews or seen them on <a href="https://youtu.be/oTO8InO6dU8">Channel 4, Steph's Packed Lunch</a>, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PuEJW6mL-m8">BBC Look East</a>, <a href="https://www.northamptonchron.co.uk/arts-and-culture/books/two-northampton-schoolgirl-sisters-launch-monthly-book-subscription-boxes-after-publishing-their-debut-novels-3170503">Northampton Chronicle &amp; Echo</a>, <a href="https://www.mirror.co.uk/money/young-entrepreneurs-aged-just-11-23499616">Daily Express, Daily Mirror</a>, <a href="https://archive.thestrategist.co.uk/article/black-owned-uk-businesses.html">The Strategist</a>, <a href="https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/health-and-families/leah-williamson-moana-elsa-children-research-b2158251.html">The Independent</a>, The WeekJnr magazine or even <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oQavwisW2SI">Disney</a>.&nbsp;<br><br>In marketing their books, we realised there was a gap in the market for children's book subscriptions with diverse and inclusive books which also keeps reluctant and struggling readers. This is how the idea of Happier Every Chapter, a book subscription box for kids 0-14 was borne.&nbsp;<br><br><span style="font-weight: bold;">Our dream? The vision? To help schools and families nurture the skill and will to read for pleasure while developing a solid global outlook. </span>Thanks to the subscribers and schools making <span style="color: rgb(22, 41, 80);"><a href="https://www.happiereverychapter.com">Happier Every Chapter</a>,</span>&nbsp;their go-to for inclusive and value-rich children's bestsellers.</span></p></div>
    </div>
  </div></div></div>
</section>  </section>  
